{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1171005-how-could-this-part-of-my-antagonist-s-backstory-work","id":1171005,"title":"How could this part of my antagonist's backstory work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-27T11:37:09-08:00","id":1171005,"title":"How could this part of my antagonist's backstory work?","content":"As part of my New Orleans chronicle, i though up a Ma Barker-style antagonist who runs a criminal entetprise called The Greenwood Clan. Ma Greenwood herself is a nasty, wyrm tainted old woman of about 80 years. She and her 2 sons run the Clan's criminal enterprise with a iron fist and makes sure that their actions bring as much taint as possible.<br /> <br /> One part of Ma's backstory has her claim that she visited Malfeas. Could that be possible and if so, how could that have effected her and her Clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T08:32:55-08:00","id":1171242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1171005-how-could-this-part-of-my-antagonist-s-backstory-work#post1171005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As part of my New Orleans chronicle, i though up a Ma Barker-style antagonist who runs a criminal entetprise called The Greenwood Clan. Ma Greenwood herself is a nasty, wyrm tainted old woman of about 80 years. She and her 2 sons run the Clan's criminal enterprise with a iron fist and makes sure that their actions bring as much taint as possible.<br /> <br /> One part of Ma's backstory has her claim that she visited Malfeas. Could that be possible and if so, how could that have effected her and her Clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything is possible. A Black Spiral Theurge of sufficient rank could take a human into the umbra.<br /> <br /> So, assuming you have a person brought into the bowels of Malfeas, that leaves a fair few questions.<br /> <br /> Do you just want this to be how she was turned irrevocably evil? Why would she be brought there, and how did she come back? I am assuming some potent Wyrm entity allowed, maybe one of the Maeljin/Urge Wyrms or even Number 2. Once back on earth, her criminal activities fed her patron's appetites on a grand scale. Off the top of my head, The Urge Wyrm Mahsstrac might be for a fitting master (his ties with Green Dragon means tossing in some allied Black Spiral Dancers is not out outside the realm of possibility). Vorus or Angu (and by extension, their avatars and proxies) could work also. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T20:02:52-08:00","id":1171424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1171005-how-could-this-part-of-my-antagonist-s-backstory-work?p=1171242#post1171242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything is possible. A Black Spiral Theurge of sufficient rank could take a human into the umbra.<br /> <br /> So, assuming you have a person brought into the bowels of Malfeas, that leaves a fair few questions.<br /> <br /> Do you just want this to be how she was turned irrevocably evil? Why would she be brought there, and how did she come back? I am assuming some potent Wyrm entity allowed, maybe one of the Maeljin/Urge Wyrms or even Number 2. Once back on earth, her criminal activities fed her patron's appetites on a grand scale. Off the top of my head, The Urge Wyrm Mahsstrac might be for a fitting master (his ties with Green Dragon means tossing in some allied Black Spiral Dancers is not out outside the realm of possibility). Vorus or Angu (and by extension, their avatars and proxies) could work also.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is that Ma Greenwood and her husband, Ezekiel, visited Malfeas due to the fact that they were high-ranking members of a secret society that tried to resurrect the Society of the Weeping Moon and that they had to visit Malfeas to gain the favor of a Urge Wyrm or Maeljin, By this point, Ezekiel was already a successful crime boss and Ma was jealous of the power he had and decided, she wanted it for herself. So, she ended up murdering her husband in Malfeas, thus getting the attention of either Angu or Mahsstrac, who immediately claimed Ma as a servant. One twist i was thinking was that Ma sent her two sons to Malfeas, via a BSD Thurge, to also gain the favor of Angu or Mahsstrac. But, to her dismay, her sons got the attention of two different Maeljin. Zeke Jr, a sadistic bastard who helped run Ma's drug enterprise, ended up getting Lady Aife's favor while Johnny, her younger son, ended up getting the favor of Empress Aliara. Thus, of course, resulted in the two sons becoming rivals, both wanting to control the family business after Ma passes away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T11:04:58-08:00","id":1172029,"title":"","content":"Might be a stupid question, but worth asking. Are they BSD's kinfolk or are they simply chummy, poor-excuses of a human being?<br /> <br /> That could influence the focus of the motive/resources available","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}